0..70 Comment "// What a motive refuses when its body writes a type with no `return`."
71..73 Comment "//"
74..148 Comment "// A type family\'s application in a computation\'s place must refuse by its"
149..224 Comment "// sort, as a type atom does. A refusal by name or by a constructor\'s arity"
225..262 Comment "// sends the reader to the wrong fix."
263..265 Comment "//"
266..340 Comment "// Each definition below writes a family\'s application as its body with no"
341..412 Comment "// `return`. Each refuses as `OutOfFragment.WrongSort`, and the refusal"
413..433 Comment "// advises `return`."
434..436 Comment "//"
437..452 Comment "// - see: #6491"
